-- int-tests-appeal: headline (f), whole scenarios across groups G4 (the decision on an application, and the name), G2 (the charity test at two times, IP9), G8 (Article 33 and 36), G7 (Article 38: the date of the
-- notice; commencement) and, for the first scenario, the whole chain of headline (a): an application is refused, the refusal is appealed.  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from Articles 33, 36 and 38 before this
-- module was run:
--   Article 33(1): an applicant for registration may appeal a decision to refuse to register it, or to refuse to register it in the restricted section; 33(2): a registered charity may appeal five named decisions
--   (to deregister it; to refuse permission to change its name; to require it to apply to change its name; to refuse approval of an amendment of its purposes; to refuse approval of an amendment of its public benefit
--   statement); 33(3): a person served with a notice under Article 26 or a required steps notice may appeal the requirement; 33(4): the Attorney General may appeal any decision; 33(5): any other person may appeal a
--   decision to register an applicant on the ground that, at BOTH the time of the application and the time of the appeal, the applicant did not meet the charity test, or (for an appellant with an interest in the
--   registered name) the name was undesirable under Article 12(1). Article 36(2): the Minister may by Order prescribe time limits within which appeals are to be brought and provide for the giving of notice of decisions.
--   Article 38: the Minister may by Order make further provision as to the service of notices.  No Order under Article 36(2) or 38 is among the sources: the limits in these scenarios are illustrations of an Order.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (f): scenarios`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

-- A decision of the Commissioner that a group produced; a refusal to answer if the group answered NOTHING.
GIVEN d IS A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision, if the group produced one
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision that was produced` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
      WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "the deciding group produced no decision"
      WHEN JUST decision THEN decision

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the applicant company` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        standing IS `an applicant for registration`
        purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`))
        facts IS `Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun")

GIVEN a IS AN `Appellant under Article 33` @desc The appellant
      decision IS A `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision appealed
      own IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration
GIVETH AN `Appeal under Article 33`
`an appeal by` a `against` decision `concerning the appellant's own affairs` own MEANS
    `Appeal under Article 33` WITH appellant IS a, `decision appealed` IS decision, `the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration` IS own

GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`an applicant for registration appealing` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS TRUE, `a registered charity` IS FALSE, `the Attorney General` IS FALSE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`a registered charity appealing` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS FALSE, `a registered charity` IS TRUE, `the Attorney General` IS FALSE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`the Attorney General appealing` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS FALSE, `a registered charity` IS FALSE, `the Attorney General` IS TRUE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Appellant under Article 33`
`a stranger with an interest in the name appealing` MEANS
    `Appellant under Article 33` WITH `an applicant for registration` IS FALSE, `a registered charity` IS FALSE, `the Attorney General` IS FALSE, `a person served with the notice that contains the requirement` IS FALSE, `a person with an interest in the registered name of the applicant` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Notice of a decision in the case`
`the notice sent on 5 October and received on 7 October 2026` MEANS
    `Notice of a decision in the case` WITH `date sent` IS YMD 2026 10 5, `date received` IS JUST (YMD 2026 10 7), `date fixed by an Order under Article 38` IS NOTHING

GIVEN appellant IS AN `Appellant under Article 33` @desc The appellant
      decision IS A `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision
      own IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it concerns the appellant's own affairs
      lodged IS A DATE @desc The day the appeal was lodged
      limit IS A MAYBE `Time limit prescribed under Article 36(2)(a)` @desc The limit
      thenFacts IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The charity test facts at the time of the application
      nowFacts IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The charity test facts at the time of the appeal
GIVETH AN `Appeal case`
`an appeal case` appellant decision own lodged limit thenFacts nowFacts MEANS
    `Appeal case` WITH
        appeal IS `an appeal by` appellant `against` decision `concerning the appellant's own affairs` own
        body IS `the applicant company`
        `charity test facts at the time of the application` IS thenFacts
        `charity test facts at the time of the appeal` IS nowFacts
        `opinion on the name at the time of the application` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `opinion on the name at the time of the appeal` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `day of the decision` IS YMD 2026 10 2
        notice IS JUST `the notice sent on 5 October and received on 7 October 2026`
        `day the appeal was lodged` IS lodged
        limit IS limit

GIVETH A `Time limit prescribed under Article 36(2)(a)`
`an Order prescribing 28 days` MEANS `an Order prescribes a time limit of days` 28

GIVETH A `Facts for the charity test in the case`
`facts where public benefit is provided` MEANS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`
GIVETH A `Facts for the charity test in the case`
`facts where public benefit is not provided` MEANS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is not provided`

§§ `F1: the whole chain -- an application is refused (headline (a)) and the applicant appeals (headline (f))`

-- The applicant of scenario A5 (a political-party purpose) is refused; the decision is the one headline (a) produced (IP27). The applicant may appeal a refusal to register (Article 33(1)(a)).
GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the refused application` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `Body in the case` WITH
            name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
            standing IS `an applicant for registration`
            purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`)), (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` `Int fx a political party purpose`)
            facts IS `Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))
            model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
            people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun")
        `charity test facts` IS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`
        application IS `Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        findings IS `Int fx clear findings`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS `Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision on the refused application` MEANS
    `the decision that was produced` ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the refused application`)'s decision)

#ASSERT `the decision on the refused application` EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) (JUST `an Order prescribing 28 days`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the right of appeal` EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(1)(a)`
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) (JUST `an Order prescribing 28 days`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the person may appeal the decision`

§§ `F2: by when -- Article 36(2) and the date of the notice (Article 38)`

-- The notice was sent on 5 October and received on 7 October 2026. On the favoured reading of F7.7 the notice is served on the date of receipt, 7 October. An Order (here, an illustration) allows 28 days from the
-- notice of the decision (F8.6, reading taken), not counting the day of the notice (F8.12, reading taken): the last day is 4 November 2026.
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) (JUST `an Order prescribing 28 days`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the date on which the notice of the decision is served` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 7)
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) (JUST `an Order prescribing 28 days`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the last day to bring the appeal` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 11 4)
-- Lodged on 4 November: in time. Lodged on 5 November: out of time.
#ASSERT `Int (f) was the appeal brought in time` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) (JUST `an Order prescribing 28 days`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`)
#ASSERT NOT `Int (f) was the appeal brought in time` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 5) (JUST `an Order prescribing 28 days`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`)
-- No Order supplied: the sources do not say whether the appeal is in time, and the model refuses; the right of appeal itself is still answered, with no last day.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (f) was the appeal brought in time` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 5) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`)
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 5) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the last day to bring the appeal` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An Order that prescribes no limit: the appeal cannot be out of time.
#ASSERT `Int (f) was the appeal brought in time` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (JUST `no Order has prescribed a time limit`) `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`)

§§ `F3: a registered charity -- five named decisions only -- and the Attorney General -- any decision`

GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision to deregister the charity` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the refusal of the restricted section to a general section charity` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`, `the Commissioner refuses`
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`a decision on any other matter` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `any other matter`, `the Commissioner refuses`

#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a registered charity appealing` `the decision to deregister the charity` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the right of appeal` EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(2)(a)`
-- Trap T12 (reading taken, F8.4): a charity in the general section whose request for the restricted section is refused is not an "applicant for registration", and its decision is not among the five of 33(2): Part 8 gives no appeal.
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a registered charity appealing` `the refusal of the restricted section to a general section charity` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the right of appeal` EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a registered charity appealing` `the refusal of the restricted section to a general section charity` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the person may appeal the decision`
-- The Attorney General may appeal any decision (Article 33(4)), including the one no one else may.
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `the Attorney General appealing` `the refusal of the restricted section to a general section charity` FALSE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the right of appeal` EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(4)`
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `the Attorney General appealing` `a decision on any other matter` FALSE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the person may appeal the decision`

§§ `F4: a third party appeals a decision to register -- Article 33(5)(a) -- the charity test must fail at BOTH times (IP9)`

-- The decision appealed is a decision to register (the Commissioner did what was sought). At the time of the application the determination found no public benefit, so the applicant did not meet the charity test;
-- at the time of the appeal the determination finds public benefit, so it does. The ground needs both times: no right. If it failed at both times, the right is Article 33(5)(a).
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision to register` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`

#ASSERT NOT ((`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a stranger with an interest in the name appealing` `the decision to register` FALSE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is not provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application`)
#ASSERT ((`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a stranger with an interest in the name appealing` `the decision to register` FALSE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is not provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a stranger with an interest in the name appealing` `the decision to register` FALSE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is not provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`))'s `the person may appeal the decision`
#ASSERT (`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`an appeal case` `a stranger with an interest in the name appealing` `the decision to register` FALSE (YMD 2026 11 4) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is not provided` `facts where public benefit is not provided`))'s `the right of appeal` EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(a)`

§§ `F5: the day -- Part 8 (other than Article 32) came into force on 1 May 2018`

-- On 30 April 2018 Article 5 (Part 3, from 21 November 2014) is in force and Article 12 (Part 4, from 1 May 2018) is the first in the list that is not.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (f) who may appeal the decision` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) (`an appeal case` `an applicant for registration appealing` `the decision on the refused application` TRUE (YMD 2018 6 1) NOTHING `facts where public benefit is provided` `facts where public benefit is provided`) BECAUSE "Article 12 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
